   "Recorded nondeterminism, replay equality, no undeclared duplicated external effect, REPL grant denial. R6/R7/R8/R9: topology/provider/event-log/state/message schemas; durable idempotency, timeout/retry/cancellation/failure/compensation records; migration or rejection of replay-incompatible code/topology/schema changes; model/provider/prompt provenance, output and sink validation, policy-recorded provider substitution, typed tool contracts with caller/callee grants and policy-required human review, memory/retrieval privacy/retention/deletion/taint controls and secret redaction; R7/R8 replay-required segments return recorded model/tool/retrieval/memory/review decisions or reject a missing record. R6 concurrency fixtures accept an authorized graph-declared replay-safe repetition where no R7/R8 recorded-output obligation applies; the declaration never grants authority or overrides those recorded-output obligations. Interactive forms and generated code pass the ordinary compiler checks before execution; session manifests, transcripts, evaluated forms, syntax/core/MIR/source snapshots capture build-affecting state or mark nonhermeticity, and hot reload invalidates stale analysis/backend/runtime/package outputs. Reject undeclared repeated external calls, live nondeterministic calls in R7/R8 recorded-output segments even with a replay-safe graph declaration, repetitions without required authority, unvalidated trusted sinks, forbidden-profile eval, hidden interactive IO and stale reload artifacts. Dependencies: Domains supplies agent/workflow contracts, Schema supplies validators/migrations, Build consumes session inputs and invalidation, Auth supplies grants and review policy. Project work/token/call/time/retry allowances are removed admission requirements; actual provider billing/account limits remain external, and semantic failure/cancellation policy remains required. R8 mixed budget spans retain unresolved qualification in the family proposal.. Under [SAFE8/SAFE13](../../docs/phase-02-safety/README.md), retain signal/timer/retry/idempotency/compensation and tool failure records; exact replay consumes recorded model/tool outputs, while audit policy retains digests, schemas, decisions, review events and providers. None is allowed only in interactive or non-safe contexts; workflow and release claims require replay or audit. Execute retention/deletion and secret-tainted memory denial fixtures through the declared provider; prompt text never grants authority. Residual criterion runtime/hot-reload-invalidation: For a changed interactive definition, record changed source, affected namespace/dependency edges and invalidation of stale syntax, analysis, typed core, MIR/domain IR, backend, runtime and package artifacts. Emit a hot-reload/session record distinguishing preserved runtime state from state that must restart, with evaluated-form/source/generated-origin identity. Show an unaffected artifact retained and affected artifacts rebuilt or rejected before reuse; reject a stale analysis/MIR/backend/runtime/package artifact, untracked build-affecting state and debug inspection outside grants/secret policy. Build-affecting session inputs are captured or explicitly nonhermetic; interactive manifests do not imply release runtime support. Build-affecting sessions emit transcripts, evaluated-form artifacts, syntax/core/MIR snapshots, dependency invalidation records and source maps; debug hooks cannot expose raw memory, host process state or model/tool outputs without grants. Source obligation `language/effects/interpret-tool-call`: Interpret a tool call against its declared schema, tool identity, human-review and authority policy, returning a typed result without ambient tool privilege. Accept: Interpret ai/tool-call through the declared tool identity and input/output schema, effects, capability and policy-required human review; validate and return a typed result with original effect/handler identity. Preserve actual external provider/account policy without introducing project work quotas. Reject: Reject schema/type mismatch, unknown tool, missing grant/review or ambient tool authority; a handler declaration cannot create authority. Required outputs: Typed tool-handler artifacts, schema validation, grant/review decisions, result/replay records and accepted/rejected fixtures. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/effects/interpret-workflow-replay`: Interpret workflow event/replay operations and their time/random/activity/model/tool/review/retry/compensation records under the durable replay contract. Accept: Record workflow/event and workflow/replay operations with stable event/step identity, input/output schemas, effects, external results, time/random/activity/model/tool/review/retry/compensation decisions and replay IDs. Record mode writes and replay mode reads; concurrent branches replay deterministically with original handler labels/identity. Preserve R6 graph-declared replay-safe operations only where no R7/R8 recorded-output obligation applies. Reject: Reject missing/mismatched/reordered replay records, live nondeterministic work in recorded-output segments and silent repetition of external effects; emit L11-REPLAY-RACE when durable concurrency lacks a record. Required outputs: Typed handler/event/step graph, replay log, record-versus-replay traces, deterministic branch comparison and refusal diagnostics. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/errors/emit-ai-policy-failure`: Emit structured audit/policy evidence for AI/model/tool/schema/defense/review failure instead of losing it in exception text. Accept: Emit structured policy/audit artifacts for model-provider failure, tool failure, schema validation, policy denial, prompt-defense trigger and human-review denial, preserving source spans and generated-origin chains. Actual external account/billing errors may remain explicit; removed project quotas are not restored. Reject: Reject free-text-only or missing AI/tool failure evidence, omitted policy/schema/review identity and lost source/generated origins; report L9-AI-ERROR. Required outputs: Typed AI/tool failure record, policy/audit/replay links, validation/denial fixtures and source-bound diagnostics. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/errors/emit-durable-workflow-failure`: Emit and replay a durable workflow failure record with its step/input/error identity, retry/compensation policy and external-result/replay provenance. Accept: Persist and replay a workflow failure with step ID, input and output/error schemas, retry/compensation policy, time, external-call results and replay ID; retain source/generated origins and exercise failure plus compensation replay. Reject: Reject workflow failure without durable record, missing required schema/policy/result/replay identity or live re-execution during recorded replay; report L9-WORKFLOW-ERROR. Required outputs: Durable typed failure and compensation records, replay equality/refusal fixtures and source/generated-origin diagnostic artifacts. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from eff